{
  "_help": [
    "What is in the Sprout Lands pack. Read by build_assets.py; see tools/assets/README.md.",
    "tilesets: every sheet that can be painted in Tiled (16x16 grid). 'terrain' turns on terrain (Wang) detection:",
    "  a name for the whole sheet, or a list of {name, rows: [first, last]} when a sheet holds several terrains.",
    "  'layoutFrom' takes the pieces from a clean cut-out sheet with the same layout (for sheets whose outlines confuse",
    "  the detection), 'wang' sets pieces by hand, 'terrainExclude' skips tiles, 'animations' makes animated tiles.",
    "sprites: animation sheets. 'frame' is the frame size, 'offset' where the grid starts, 'rows' names each row",
    "  ('auto' = row_00, row_01 ...; a list or {row: name} for real names), 'duration' is ms per frame,",
    "  'variants' lists sheets with the same layout (colours), 'rowCount' stops after that many rows (when a sheet",
    "  switches to another grid further down, add a second entry with its own 'offset'). Empty frames are skipped.",
    "  'anchor': [x, y] (pixels of a frame, from its top left) is the point drawn on the tile's middle, for sheets whose",
    "  character isn't in the middle of its frame (default: the frame's middle).",
    "ignore: files that are neither (previews, duplicates). Paths are relative to the pack directory.",
    "'door animation sprites.png' is a tileset only, not a sprite sheet: its frames overlap (a 3px pillar + the door",
    "  leaf every 16px), so no grid cuts them right. Animating doors needs frames given as rectangles (not supported yet)."
  ],
